{"sourceSha256": "6574625159d2940e7e14b603f32fce7772256ca6902c4883023f8502a0cc6845", "text": "Ticket Id: 25703\n\nDr. George Isaacson\n\nCardiologist\n\n45 Inkerman Street\n\nCaulfield 3162\n\n19/1/2007\n\nDear Dr.Isaacson,\n\nRE: Mr. Jing Zu\n\nI am writing to refer Mr Zu, a 72-year-old retired school teacher whose features are suggestive of ischemic   Comment [teacher1]: worsening\nheart disease.\n\nMr. Zu has been suffering from hypertension, ischemic heart disease and congestive heart failure for many\nyears. Accordingly, he has been commenced on Lasix, Arginine, enalapril and nifedipine.                       Comment [teacher2]: a\n\nOn 3/1/20117, Mr. Zu firstly presented with angina on exertion which was neither relieved with Arginine\nnor resting. His examination was unremarkable apart from hypertension (blood pressure was 160/90) and         Comment [teacher3]: arginine and\nbilateral basal crepitations. On 15/1/2007, his condition deteriorated. He came complaining of progressive\ndyspnea and orthopnea .His examination revealed lower limb edema up to the knees in addition to chest\ncrepitations extending to the middle lung zones. Consequently, Lasix dose was increased to 80 mg.\n\nToday, the patient presented with a history of angina episode on mild exertion which lasted for 10 minutes\nyesterday. However, his complaint of dyspnea decreased. ECG confirmed anterolateral myocardial\nischemic changes.\n\nIn view of the above, I would appreciate if you provide an assessment of Mr Zu and advice regarding           Comment [teacher4]: as well as the\ntreatment and management his condition as you see suitable. Should you have any queries, please do not        Comment [teacher5]: of\nhesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n\n                                     Report\n Word length                  194\n Comments                     This is a well written letter but some case\n                              interpretation errors are visible.\n Estimate